        "payload": "tree 602e19e23bfe0bf6a52b9370b5067e52b757c347\nparent 067b38d530d2a43f62b1c2b8ea7308976d6a0c6e\nauthor Rob Woodgate <robwoodgate@users.noreply.github.com> 1778248282 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778248282 +0100\n\nfix(wallet): treat expiry: 0 as no-expiry in validateMintQuote (#648)\n\nCDK emits expiry: 0 on mint quote responses to mean \"no expiry\"; the\nspec defines expiry as <int|null> where null is \"no expiry\". cashu-ts\nwas reading 0 as a real Unix timestamp (epoch 1970) and rejecting all\nsuch quotes as expired.\n\nTreat 0 as the null case so wallets can mint against CDK without\nhitting \"Mint quote ... has expired\" on quotes the mint considers\nperpetually valid. Adds a unit test pinning the new behaviour.\n\nAffects all mint methods (bolt11/bolt12/onchain) since validateMintQuote\nis method-agnostic.",
